5092a6c5-e5f1-4e1e-b4b6-a7dd2f2af822.projectDescriptionBackground:
The aim of the project was to enhance climate change education at universities throughout Eastern, Central and Western Europe. It is well known that greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions in the atmosphere are at high levels. This situation requires clear steps to be taken to reduce the impact of climate change as a result of human activity. One of the essential step is to increase awareness, knowledge and opportunities towards carbon neutrality. Hi-EduCarbon is just such an educational course and scheme that has provided new knowledge in: 
•	Determining the greenhouse gas emissions and removals on the level of product - building materials and building services;
•	Determining the greenhouse gas emissions and removals on the level of product - structures and whole building;
•	Determining the greenhouse gas emissions and removals on the level of organization, neighbourhoods and cities.

results.resultDescription:
The recreate platform has been prepared to support the development of entrepreneurial attitude skills. To this end, the consortium developed a modular training course that can be used to organize workshops on specific topics related to entrepreneurship and knowledge transfer. The platform implements entrepreneurship topics in the following areas:
1) Risk taking;
2) Marketing;
3) Leadership;
4) Business planning;
5) Startup Founding;

The workshop approach allows universities to easily use the entire course or part of it. The newly developed learning environment and its tools is based on the methodology of mixing traditional training approach (the training modules) with informal learning: simulations, educational games are in fact meant to favor the acquisition of key competences through non-traditional methods.
