The main goal of this output has been to define detailed guidelines and advices for the preparation of the two specific learning paths provided by AuToMa project (one more technical and another one more managerial). A professional learning contents design and planning approach has been considered for the 20 learning modules design. The guidelines for the learning contents development were developed by LUISS University, thanks its rich experience in preparation and implementation of different learning approaches. The main tasks that have been developed are the following:
- A needs analysis of the target groups (e.g. previous knowledge and skills, geographical provenience, learning context and access to technology);
- Specific learning needs and job-related skills identification;
- A set of the best learning objectives required to achieve the general and high-level courses objectives;
- A set of instructional, media, evaluation and delivery strategies useful for AuToMa learning goals.
